# A prompt in here is evidence. Its size in characters, its diff against the previous capture and
# any hash taken over it are all byte-level facts, and Git's newline conversion rewrites those
# bytes on a Windows checkout. Normalise to LF in the index and check out LF everywhere, so a
# clone on any platform holds the same bytes the harness sent.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
